<country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, NAOYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIE, TOMOYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUBARA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An absorption refrigerating machine of a type in which cooling water flows parallelly through an absorber and a condenser, wherein plate type heat exchangers (H1, H3) are used for the absorber (A) and condenser (C), the arrangement being such that the amounts of cooling water distributed between the absorber and the condenser are determined mainly by the respective fluid resistances of the plate type heat exchangers.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Machine frigorifique à absorption dans laquelle le liquide réfrigérant passe parallèlement dans un absorbeur et dans un condenseur. Des échangeurs thermiques (H1, H3) à plaques sont utilisés pour l'absorbeur (A) et le condenseur (C). L'agencement est tel que la quantité de liquide réfrigérant passant soit dans l'absorbeur, soit dans le condenseur est déterminée principalement par la résistance fluidique des échangeurs thermiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-f